  "$comment": "Fake secrets shared by every Psyche test. NONE of these values is real. They exist so the secret-leak checker (packages/testing secrets.ts, `pnpm check:secrets`) can prove that no vault value, card, bank account or government identifier ever reaches model-visible text, logs, transcripts, receipts or notifications (docs/05 §4.5–§4.7, §15.4 item 7). Token shapes deliberately avoid real provider prefixes so GitHub push protection and real scanners do not fire. Card numbers are the payment networks' published test numbers. See README.md in this folder before adding entries. Secret values are stored as {\"derive\": {prefix, alphabet, length}} recipes and materialized by derive.mjs (and packages/testing secret-registry.ts), so no secret-looking literal is committed.",
